1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,047
Welcome to the capstone!

2
00:00:02,047 --> 00:00:05,013
You've learned each part
of Kyntlo on its own.

3
00:00:05,013 --> 00:00:09,849
Now we'll connect them into one system
that turns a stranger into a booked,

4
00:00:09,849 --> 00:00:12,170
happy customer, mostly on autopilot.

5
00:00:12,170 --> 00:00:15,781
We'll follow one real lead,
Olivia, all the way through.

6
00:00:16,635 --> 00:00:18,960
Here's the whole system in one line.

7
00:00:18,960 --> 00:00:20,704
A funnel attracts the lead.

8
00:00:20,704 --> 00:00:22,642
A form captures their details.

9
00:00:22,642 --> 00:00:26,906
A workflow replies instantly, and
creates a deal in your pipeline.

10
00:00:26,906 --> 00:00:31,104
The calendar takes the booking,
reminders make sure they turn up,

11
00:00:31,104 --> 00:00:34,851
and a review request turns a
good visit into social proof.

12
00:00:35,700 --> 00:00:36,975
It starts in Sites.

13
00:00:36,975 --> 00:00:40,600
Bloom runs a funnel called
Invisalign Free Scan Offer.

14
00:00:40,600 --> 00:00:43,016
Their Facebook ads send people here.

15
00:00:43,016 --> 00:00:48,654
The page explains the offer, and has one
clear call to action: claim your free scan.

16
00:00:49,503 --> 00:00:52,999
On that funnel sits the
Invisalign Enquiry form.

17
00:00:52,999 --> 00:00:58,242
Every submission creates or updates
a contact in your CRM automatically.

18
00:00:58,242 --> 00:01:01,883
This form has already
captured over 400 enquiries.

19
00:01:02,734 --> 00:01:05,880
The moment Olivia submits
it, this workflow fires.

20
00:01:05,880 --> 00:01:07,831
Its trigger is that exact form.

21
00:01:07,831 --> 00:01:12,990
It creates her deal in the pipeline, texts
her within seconds with a booking link,

22
00:01:12,990 --> 00:01:15,822
and alerts the team
member who owns the lead.

23
00:01:16,671 --> 00:01:20,716
In Opportunities, Olivia's
deal is waiting in New Enquiry,

24
00:01:20,716 --> 00:01:23,784
with its value and
source already filled in.

25
00:01:23,784 --> 00:01:25,318
Nobody typed anything.

26
00:01:25,318 --> 00:01:30,828
When she books, the pipeline workflow
from lesson 9.5 moves her to Consultation

27
00:01:30,828 --> 00:01:31,316
Booked.

28
00:01:32,166 --> 00:01:35,025
The link in her text opens
your booking calendar.

29
00:01:35,025 --> 00:01:38,351
She picks a time that suits
her, and it lands right here,

30
00:01:38,351 --> 00:01:41,968
in the right person's calendar,
with no back-and-forth emails.

31
00:01:42,822 --> 00:01:45,513
Booking triggers the appointment workflow.

32
00:01:45,513 --> 00:01:50,638
Olivia gets an instant confirmation, then
reminders the day before and two hours

33
00:01:50,638 --> 00:01:51,087
before.

34
00:01:51,087 --> 00:01:54,226
This is the part that
protects you from no-shows.

35
00:01:54,226 --> 00:01:58,583
And if she does miss it, the no-show
workflow offers her a new time.

36
00:01:59,433 --> 00:02:03,030
After her visit, the team marks
the appointment as showed.

37
00:02:03,030 --> 00:02:06,503
Two hours later, this workflow
asks Olivia for a review,

38
00:02:06,503 --> 00:02:08,736
while the experience is still fresh.

39
00:02:09,586 --> 00:02:11,877
Those reviews flow into Reputation.

40
00:02:11,877 --> 00:02:15,477
More happy customers leave
reviews, your rating climbs,

41
00:02:15,477 --> 00:02:19,077
and your next ad brings in
even more leads like Olivia.

42
00:02:19,077 --> 00:02:22,284
That's the loop that makes
the whole system grow.

43
00:02:23,133 --> 00:02:26,347
Before you trust any system,
test it as a customer.

44
00:02:26,347 --> 00:02:29,686
Fill in your own form, then
open your contact record.

45
00:02:29,686 --> 00:02:34,412
The activity timeline should show every
step: the form, the tags, the deal,

46
00:02:34,412 --> 00:02:36,744
and every message the workflows sent.

47
00:02:37,595 --> 00:02:38,988
Finally, watch it work.

48
00:02:38,988 --> 00:02:42,684
Your dashboard shows how many
leads came in, how many booked,

49
00:02:42,684 --> 00:02:45,168
and how much revenue the system produced.

50
00:02:45,168 --> 00:02:49,045
If one number dips, you now know
exactly which piece to look at.

51
00:02:49,894 --> 00:02:50,969
Here's a pro tip.

52
00:02:50,969 --> 00:02:53,500
Don't build everything in one afternoon.

53
00:02:53,500 --> 00:02:57,105
Add one link of the chain,
test it with your own details,

54
00:02:57,105 --> 00:02:58,813
and only then add the next.

55
00:02:58,813 --> 00:03:02,482
A simple system that works
beats a clever one that breaks.

56
00:03:03,333 --> 00:03:07,895
That's a complete lead-to-booking system,
built from everything you've learned.

57
00:03:07,895 --> 00:03:10,955
In the final lesson, I'll
give you a thirty-day plan,

58
00:03:10,955 --> 00:03:13,322
so you know exactly what to set up first.

59
00:03:13,322 --> 00:03:14,131
See you there!
